% transferOwnership
% reverts: Ownable: new owner is the zero address
it must not be true that
    an owner hands the ownership to a second owner
    and the second owner is equal to the zero address.

% reverts: Ownable: caller is not the owner
it must not be true that
    an owner hands the ownership to a second owner
    and the owner of the token is an account
    and the owner is different from the account.

when an owner hands the ownership to a second owner
    and the owner of the token is an account
then it is not the case that the owner of the token is the account.

when an owner hands the ownership to a second owner
then the owner of the token is the second owner.

% pause
% reverts: Pausable: caller is not the pauser
it must not be true that
    a pauser pauses the token
    and the pauser of the token is an account
    and the pauser is different from the account.

when a pauser pauses the token
then the token is paused.

% unpause
% reverts: Pausable: caller is not the pauser
it must not be true that
    a pauser unpauses the token
    and the pauser of the token is an account
    and the pauser is different from the account.

when a pauser unpauses the token
then it is not the case that the token is paused.

% updatePauser
% reverts: Pausable: new pauser is the zero address
it must not be true that
    an owner appoints an account pauser
    and the account is equal to the zero address.

% reverts: Ownable: caller is not the owner
it must not be true that
    an owner appoints an account pauser
    and the owner of the token is a second account
    and the owner is different from the second account.

when an owner appoints an account pauser
    and the pauser of the token is a second account
then it is not the case that the pauser of the token is the second account.

when an owner appoints an account pauser
then the pauser of the token is the account.

% blacklist
% reverts: Blacklistable: caller is not the blacklister
it must not be true that
    a blacklister blacklists an account
    and the blacklister of the token is a second account
    and the blacklister is different from the second account.

when a blacklister blacklists an account
then the account is on the blacklist.

% unBlacklist
% reverts: Blacklistable: caller is not the blacklister
it must not be true that
    a blacklister clears an account from the blacklist
    and the blacklister of the token is a second account
    and the blacklister is different from the second account.

when a blacklister clears an account from the blacklist
then it is not the case that the account is on the blacklist.

% updateBlacklister
% reverts: Blacklistable: new blacklister is the zero address
it must not be true that
    an owner appoints an account blacklister
    and the account is equal to the zero address.

% reverts: Ownable: caller is not the owner
it must not be true that
    an owner appoints an account blacklister
    and the owner of the token is a second account
    and the owner is different from the second account.

when an owner appoints an account blacklister
    and the blacklister of the token is a second account
then it is not the case that the blacklister of the token is the second account.

when an owner appoints an account blacklister
then the blacklister of the token is the account.

% mint
% reverts: Panic 0x11 (arithmetic overflow or underflow)
it must not be true that
    a minter mints an amount for a recipient
    and the total supply is a second amount
    and second amount + amount > the largest amount.

% reverts: Panic 0x11 (arithmetic overflow or underflow)
it must not be true that
    a minter mints an amount for a recipient
    and the balance of the recipient is a second amount
    and second amount + amount > the largest amount.

% reverts: FiatToken: mint amount exceeds minterAllowance
it must not be true that
    a minter mints an amount for a recipient
    and the minting allowance of the minter is a second amount
    and the amount > the second amount.

% reverts: FiatToken: mint amount not greater than 0
it must not be true that
    a minter mints an amount for a recipient
    and the amount <= 0.

% reverts: FiatToken: mint to the zero address
it must not be true that
    a minter mints an amount for a recipient
    and the recipient is equal to the zero address.

% reverts: Blacklistable: account is blacklisted
it must not be true that
    a minter mints an amount for a recipient
    and the recipient is on the blacklist.

% reverts: Blacklistable: account is blacklisted
it must not be true that
    a minter mints an amount for a recipient
    and the minter is on the blacklist.

% reverts: FiatToken: caller is not a minter
it must not be true that
    a minter mints an amount for a recipient
    and it is not the case that the minter is a minter of the token.

% reverts: Pausable: paused
it must not be true that
    a minter mints an amount for a recipient
    and the token is paused.

when a minter mints an amount for a recipient
then the total supply that is a second amount becomes second amount + amount.

when a minter mints an amount for a recipient
then the balance of the recipient that is a second amount becomes second amount + amount.

when a minter mints an amount for a recipient
then the minting allowance of the minter that is a second amount becomes second amount - amount.

% approve
% reverts: ERC20: approve to the zero address
it must not be true that
    an owner approves a spender for an amount
    and the spender is equal to the zero address.

% reverts: Blacklistable: account is blacklisted
it must not be true that
    an owner approves a spender for an amount
    and the spender is on the blacklist.

